WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:04.004
♪♪

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.214
Allie:
They found us.

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:06.215
We need to go. 

00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:07.007
♪♪

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:10.177
On the one hand Mosquito Coast
is a straight up pure adventure
story

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:12.221
Justin:
about a family that is on the
run. 

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:15.015
Justin:
And needs to get to a
destination

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.309
to gain safety for themselves
and their family.

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:20.812
But the other story is a very
determined man who manipulated

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:25.192
his family to do things that
they wouldn't normally want to do or need
to do.

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:26.777
-Leaving where?
-America.

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:27.778
Why?

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:33.283
This family has secrets and has
problems, financial and emotional
and otherwise.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:38.413
Neil:
But, instead of leaning
further into that family drama,

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.998
we explode it.

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:42.042
(Police sirens)

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:45.045
Whatever they did in their
past they're individuals 

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.964
who raged against the machine
and now they're 

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:48.590
people who are on the run from
the law.

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:52.261
I think they're doing everything
to find a new civilization

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:54.179
Melissa:
that's gonna save them and
give them the normal life

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.639
Melissa:
that they have been dreaming
of. 

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:56.348
♪♪

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:57.349
We need to tell the kids.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:00:58.141
♪♪

00:00:58.141 --> 00:00:59.142
Margot:
They could get hurt.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.602
It'll be an education.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.146
♪♪

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.857
Allie Fox, he's an incredibly
bright man.

00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:07.651
Justin:
He's pursuing his own desires

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:09.611
Justin:
and not necessarily his
family's.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:13.156
Justin:
Sort of a fine line between doing
whats right for your family 

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:14.783
Justin:
and then being emotionally
manipulative 

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.076
Justin:
to get what you want.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.744
Allie, we're really in
trouble.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.789
And we just make the move and
we start again.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:21.873
♪♪

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:24.126
Melissa:
You look at these people that
think they're the perfect parents

00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:26.420
and they're doing the right thing
to give their children a better
life.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.254
♪♪

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:29.381
They're totally isolated from the
rest of the world.

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:32.092
Gabriel:
No internet, no technology at
all.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:35.762
And just like living as they own
tribe island basically. 

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.848
Han Solo, from the movie?

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:40.559
We don't really watch movies or
TV shows.

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:41.310
♪♪

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.894
Mostly just read books and
stuff.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:44.938
Dina has been home-schooled.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.190
Her only friends are her parents
and her brother.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.860
Login:
She's really looking for
just, structure.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.196
Login:
Because that's anything that
she has yet to have.

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:53.905
♪♪

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:56.742
I think by exposing this family

00:01:56.742 --> 00:01:59.244
to the kind of the, the furnace
of experience,

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:03.457
Neil:
We begin revealing to the viewer
and to each other 

00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:04.875
their true nature.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.418
You're better off with your
Mother and I.

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:08.003
♪♪

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:12.090
In what world? Do you know how
deranged you sound?

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.550
♪♪

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.260
Rupert:
How you deal with that
situation.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.888
Rupert:
How you respond to it both
externally and internally,

00:02:17.888 --> 00:02:19.806
I think makes for really good
story telling. 

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.682
♪♪

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:22.476
There's just something
compelling about

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:24.102
this very thrilling ride that
they're on. 

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:24.603
(Allie laughing)

00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:28.648
♪♪

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.525
Trust me, we'll be fine. 

00:02:30.525 --> 00:02:33.862
♪♪

